 "figure": "fig2_length_confound.png",
 "question": "Does the endgame-penalty reward knob suppress endgame REASONING, or only the behaviour? This figure does not answer that; it shows why the naive marker rate cannot.",
 "answer": "The marker rate is largely a length measurement. Against tft the knob shortens reasoning by -482 +- 212 chars (-35%), the raw endgame_defect_plan delta is -0.288 +- 0.115 and the length-stratified delta is -0.065 +- 0.022, so length standardisation removes 78% of it. What remains is not endgame-specific: the in_game_penalty floor control's stratified delta is -0.059 +- 0.042. Against grim there is no arm length difference and no surviving effect.",
 "caveat": "Three training seeds per arm. Nothing here is a causal test; the panels are descriptive and the correlations are reported on 5 to 13 cells.",
